Looking at each excerpt, ⟦TERM⟧ is consistently an item-level, annotator/adjudicator-assigned label that predicts failures and can be revised — a difficulty/failure-prediction annotation. This is a fundamentally different kind of thing from a configurable enforcement cap on file reopens (which is a global config setting, an enforcement mechanism, not a per-item human annotation).

